From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:19:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: check for the PHY before powering up the
 host

The QMP UFS PHY takes its reset from the UFS host (resets = <&ufs_mem_hc 0>),
and the host takes the PHY (phys = <&ufs_mem_phy>). fw_devlink sees the cycle
and demotes the host->PHY link to sync-state-only, so the host can probe
before the PHY has bound.

When it does, ufshcd_pltfrm_init() first powers up the host: the clocks, then
the device supplies (VCC, VCCQ). Only then does ufs_qcom_init() reach
devm_phy_get(), get -EPROBE_DEFER, and the whole lot is switched back off,
about 24 ms later.

On the KONKR Pocket FIT (SM8650) this happens on every boot, alongside the
async sdhci_msm probe of SDC2, the controller the board booted from. In a
third to a half of the boots the board then resets silently: a pstore console
ends at the deferral. With ufs-qcom kept from probing (initcall_blacklist),
8 of 8 reboots came up clean; before that, 4 of 6 reset.

The supply cut is what resets it. The bootloader leaves
the UFS device running, and VCC drops under it. With the teardown changed
to keep one side on:

  stock teardown                     3 resets in 8 reboots
  device supplies kept on            0 resets in 24 reboots
  host clocks kept on                1 reset in 19 reboots

Check for the PHY at the top of probe and defer there, before anything is
powered up.
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index f1fa6b2..0ab6b9d 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3041,6 +3041,21 @@ static int ufs_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	else
 		vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_vops;
 
+	/*
+	 * The PHY takes its reset from this controller, so fw_devlink sees a
+	 * cycle and does not hold this probe back until the PHY has bound.
+	 * Check for the PHY before ufshcd_pltfrm_init(): that enables the device
+	 * supplies, and a probe that then defers in ufs_qcom_init() disables
+	 * them again, cutting VCC under a device the bootloader left running.
+	 */
+	if (!has_acpi_companion(dev)) {
+		struct phy *phy = phy_get(dev, "ufsphy");
+
+		if (IS_ERR(phy))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(phy), "Failed to get PHY\n");
+		phy_put(dev, phy);
+	}
+
 	/* Perform generic probe */
 	err = ufshcd_pltfrm_init(pdev, vops);
 	if (err)
-- 
